Fresnel Strut

Ingredients: BRITISH BLUES & BLUES ROCK + SYNTHPOP & NEW ROMANTICS + EUPHORIC, ENERGETIC & JOLLY + Arpeggiator  
Creative Catalyst: Solitary lighthouse keepers broadcasting ecstatic bootleg radio transmissions to transatlantic icebreakers through six-month polar nights.

Fresnel Strut is an explosive, high-stepping collision of grit and glamour: scorching, Marshall-cranked 1960s British blues riffs and overblown harmonica runs slammed directly into hyper-caffeinated, glittering Roland synth arpeggios. Instead of the brooding despair of traditional blues or the cold detachment of synthpop, the sound is relentlessly ecstatic, manic, and celebratory—a triumphant burst of survivalist joy that turns sub-zero isolation into a dazzling, stomping theatrical revue.

