- Tempo & Pulse: 130–144 BPM. An exhilarating transformation of the traditional 12/8 blues shuffle into a driving, relentless straight-four dance groove propelled by northern-soul handclaps and mechanical 16th-note clockwork.
- Harmonic Palette: Bold Mixolydian and major pentatonic progressions infused with classic 12-bar blues turnarounds, elevated by bright, opulent major-ninth synth-brass chords and flamboyant, ascending arpeggiated runs.
- Production Signatures: 
  1. Fresnel Opto-Gate Modulation (an impossible technique where high-voltage guitar amplifier feedback is routed through an optical photoreceptor slaved to the 12-RPM rotation of an active lighthouse lens, creating rhythmic, blinding bursts of harmonic bloom).
  2. Salt-Sprayed Slapback (tape echoes driven into extreme saturation using vintage broadcast limiters to simulate the vast, acoustic rebound of maritime cliff faces).
  3. Dual-Wielded Leads (interlocking call-and-response between an overdriven Gibson Les Paul slide and a frantic, hyper-quantized analog arpeggiator).
- Dynamics: Songs explode immediately into high-energy anthems, briefly stripping down to just a chattering synthesizer sequence and a lone foot-stomp, before erupting into roaring, multi-octave vocal climaxes and blistering dual-lead solos.

